      ],
      "image": "assets/images/34524/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Press a thick layer of sugar on skin.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/cFZ7_0awlyWaPLpFXpf6bVCpYjU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/34524-baked-ham-step-2-ddmfs-3x4-180-fae101b3010844cd83f964911d9a0248.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/34524/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour 1 inch of water into the roasting pan; cover tightly with aluminum foil.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/UjL4A_Ge-_vEWRxsWrJP4AcfwMY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/34524-baked-ham-step-3-ddmfs-3x4-182-ec94a5e448af43f0aab0dbf543b050d1.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/34524/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven for 4 ½ to 5 hours. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center away from the bone should read at least 160 degrees F (72 degrees C).",
